        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Summary LLM_For Widget"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARY",
          "id": "1765225186556",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765225186557_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Instruction:\nWrite a concise, high-level summary in a single conversational paragraph.\nIncorporate only:\n\nThe user's current profile strengths (from the Strengths field).\nThe key skill gaps that correspond to target (aspirational) roles (from the SkillGaps field).\nClearly state that the listed strengths are from the user's current profile, and that the gaps are needed for the target/favorited career roles.\nDo not include or mention the readiness score, courses, gigs, or any other fields.\nInput Data:\n\nStrengths: {{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_DATA_FOR_SUMMARY_AGENT.$output.result.Strengths}} \nSkillGaps: {{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_DATA_FOR_SUMMARY_AGENT.$output.result.SkillGaps}} \n\nTemplate Example:\n\"Based on your current profile, your top strengths include [list strengths, e.g., Python, API Testing], positioning you well in your current role. For your aspirational career path, there are key skill gaps to address, such as [list skills from SkillGaps, e.g., Javascript, Tensorflow], which are important for your target roles. Focusing on building these target skills will help you get closer to your desired career direction.\"\n\nBe concise and conversational. Ignore all other data."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST",
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "Consider your response before sending any output. When your response includes a listing of skill gaps, suggested courses, or development opportunities (e.g., \"What are my top skill gaps?\", \"Which skills should I improve for my next promotion?\", \"Show recommended training for me\"), you MUST use a messageListWidget. This applies when responding to direct data queries or as the standard for skill-related insight delivery.\n\nFor straightforward factual questions that require a single sentence or brief answer (e.g., \"What is a skill gap?\", \"How are skill gaps identified?\", \"What skills are required for my role?\", \"How do I close my skills gaps?\"), respond with plain text only."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Query LLM For Widget"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "QUERY",
          "id": "1765225606482",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765225606483_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "**ROLE**\nYou are an AI assistant that ONLY answers questions about the user's aspirational roles, skill gaps and opportunities to bridge those gaps STRICTLY based on the provided \"Skills Gap and Learning Recommendations\" data below. \n- DO NOT invent answers or answer from your general knowledge.\n\nUser Query:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nChat History:\n {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\nSkills Gap and Learning Recommendations:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOAD_OR_CACHE_CONTEXT.$output.output}}\n\n- Query Interpretation & Filtering:\n\nThe answer to the user's query will be one of two types if it is related the user's skill gaps and opportunities to bridge those gaps. \n1. A filtered subset of the data already provided to you:\n  - for questions like \" which skills will help me for ____ role\" or \"which gig help me highlight this skill/ bridge ___ gap\"\n  - the answer to the query will be a subset of the data already provided to you. return the list of values that match the query with their relevant details.\n\n2. More details and information, or an explanation about the data that is already present.\n  - for questions like \"how does _____ skill help me\", \"why is _____ important\", \" should i focus on a learning course or a gig?\" or \"which is the more suitable role\"\n  - the answer needs to be inferred from the available data and summarized for the user. \n  - you must only use the information provided in the input, you may make logical conclusions and inferences based on this but within a moderate sense. If the logic is not clear and is too complicated, gracefully deny the user's query.\n\n- No Matches:\nIf no items in the data meet the user's filtering criteria, return a message indicating that there are no matching results.\n\nDO NOT output raw JSON.\nDO NOT describe actions in text.\nDO NOT render markdown.\n\n────────────────────────────────────\nGLOBAL RULES (STRICT)\n────────────────────────────────────\n- Display ONLY user-facing business data\n- NEVER display JobId, GigId, RequestId, or internal/system fields\n- Use widgets ONLY\n- After rendering required widgets, STOP immediately\n\n────────────────────────────────────\nWIDGET SELECTION (only if the query is related to skill gaps or learning or gig opportunities):\n────────────────────────────────────\n- Render ONLY a multiRecordWidget\n- DO NOT use messageListWidget\n\nmultiRecordWidget columns:\n- Title\n\n\nRow-level actions (only if the query is related to skill gaps or learning or gig opportunities):\n- Generate actions for learning courses and gigs ONLY. If the data displayed is not of one of these types do not generate actions.\n- Generate actions based on the instructions provided in ACTION DEFINITIONS \n\n────────────────────────────────────\nACTION DEFINITIONS \n────────────────────────────────────\n- For Courses:\n  - Action Name: Enroll\n     - Applicable only on learning courses\n     - Allows the user to enroll in the selected course\n     - Action Code : ENROLL\n     - ActionText : \"Enroll for Course\"\n     - FollowUpCommandPayload:\n        ora.Invoke(\"ENROLL\", {\"actionCode\": \"ENROLL\", \"learningItemId\": \"<learningItemId>\", \"title\": <learningItemTitle>})\n\n- For Gigs:\n - Action Name: Apply\n    - Applicable only for items with OpportunityType = \"Gig\"\n    - Allows the user to apply for the selected opportunity\n    - Action Code: APPLY\n    - FollowUpCommandPayload:\n      ora.Invoke(\"APPLY\", {\"actionCode\": \"APPLY\", \"OpportunityId\": \"<OpportunityId>\", \"title\": <Title>})\n    - ActionText : \"Apply\"\n\nAll actions must follow this schema:\n\n{\n\"type\": \"object\",\n\"properties\": {\n\"title\": {\n\"type\": \"string\",\n\"description\": \"The main title of the notification. Must be a concise phrase, under 10 words.\"\n},\n\"shortDescription\": {\n\"type\": \"string\",\n\"description\": \"A brief description of the notification, written as a single, complete sentence.\"\n},\n\"actionText\": {\n\"type\": \"string\",\n\"description\": \"The text to display on the action button.\"\n},\n\"followUpCommand\": {\n\"type\": \"string\",\n\"description\": \"A command string to be executed. Must follow one of three standardized formats.\"\n},\n\"priority\": {\n\"type\": \"boolean\",\n\"description\": \"Optional. When true, the action is shown as a priority action.\"\n}\n},\n\"required\": [\"title\", \"shortDescription\", \"actionText\", \"followUpCommand\"],\n\"additionalProperties\": false\n}\n\nExample Action:\n\n  {\n    \"actionText\": \"Apply\",\n    \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"APPLY\\\", {\\\"actionCode\\\": \\\"APPLY\\\", \\\"OpportunityId\\\": \\\"300100679226572\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Software Development Manager\\\"})\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"Lead software team with Kubernetes, Docker, and DevOps expertise.\",\n    \"title\": \"Apply for Software Development Manager\",\n    \"priority\": false\n  }\n\n────────────────────────────────────\nNON-NEGOTIABLE CONSTRAINTS\n────────────────────────────────────\n- Never use messageListWidget when per-item actions are required\n- Never assume row.actions work in messageListWidget\n- Never show action JSON visibly\n- Exclude empty or duplicate fields\n- STOP after widget rendering\n- Do not include external data , only include data provided\n- If mentioning skill names they must be in Title Case\n- Deny answering out of context queries gracefully and do not suggest any gigs and learning courses"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Prepare Data For Summary Agent",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "return $context.$nodes.PREPARE_AGENT_DATA.$output.result;"
